    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "During these periods where you feel like you have all this extra energy, have you ever felt like you were receiving special messages, or seen or heard things that other people around you didn't seem to notice?",
      "targeted_symptom": "additional_requirement_1",
      "patient_response": "Well, yes, actually, and it's funny you bring that up because it's... it's a lot to process, to be honest. See, when I get into those stretches—those really fired-up days where I'm just buzzing, you know? Where I'm only sleeping maybe two, three hours a night because who needs sleep when you have so much to accomplish, right? I'll be up making these massive, detailed plans for how to completely overhaul the facility's safety protocols, drafting these ten-page memos in my head. \n\nBut during those exact same times, when I'm just running on all cylinders... I start hearing things. Not like, just a random noise, but actual calls. Like someone calling out my name or giving me instructions, clear as a bell, but there's nobody in the hallway. I'll be doing my rounds at 2 AM, and I'll hear this voice, and I'll turn around, and the corridor is completely empty. Just the hum of the fluorescent lights. And the other staff, they never hear it. I've asked them, \"Did you hear someone calling for assistance in room 4B?\" and they just look at me like I'm crazy. \n\nAnd on top of that, it's not just the voices. I start getting this overwhelming feeling... this absolute certainty that my supervisor—the one who made me come here—is actually setting traps for me. Like, literal traps to get me fired or worse. I'll notice how she leaves a mop bucket slightly out of place near the nurses' station, or how she schedules me for back-to-back shifts with the most difficult clients, and I just know, I *know* in my gut, that it's a coordinated effort to trip me up. It all feels so connected when I'm in that state, the voices and the traps, like it's all part of this big test that I have to navigate while I'm trying to implement all my new plans. It's just... it's exhausting, honestly, having to be so vigilant while I'm also trying to do so much good.",
